          "id": "gen-u1-s2",
          "title": "Probability in pedigrees",
          "content": "<h3>Mechanistic foundation: Probability in pedigrees</h3>\n<p>A pedigree is a graph of biological relationships annotated by observed traits; it is not proof that one locus determines the trait. Condition each probability on the information actually observed. An unaffected person with an affected sibling has a two-thirds carrier probability for a fully penetrant autosomal recessive disorder when both parents are known carriers, because AA and Aa are the only unaffected genotypes after excluding aa. Population allele frequencies and test results may update that estimate by Bayes reasoning.</p>\n<p>For <strong>probability in pedigrees</strong>, a model written without its inheritance assumptions is not a complete explanation.</p>\n<h3>A quantitative example with a defined denominator</h3>\n<p>An unaffected sibling of an aa individual, born to two Aa parents, has P(Aa | unaffected)=2/3, not 1/2. Show the conditioning explicitly.</p>\n<p>Read the example in two passes. First solve the arithmetic as a hypothetical well-controlled classroom case. This separates a mathematical exercise from a causal scientific finding.</p>\n<h3>From the process to an experiment</h3>\n<p>Draw a three-generation synthetic pedigree with uncertain genotypes, write a likelihood for each inheritance model, and update with a molecular test whose sensitivity and specificity are stated. Specify an independent biological unit of replication. Those are different controls and answer different questions.</p>\n<p>For <strong>probability in pedigrees</strong>, interpretation should follow the biology of the observation, not merely whether a significance threshold was crossed.</p>\n<h3>Interpretations worth separating</h3>\n<p>Pedigree symbols do not encode penetrance, adoption, misattributed parentage, mosaicism or phenocopies automatically.</p>\n<p>Compare the focal mechanism with <strong>linkage and assortment</strong>, using the dedicated topic section rather than assuming these labels describe the same process. The comparison is not evidence that one causes the other. It is a deliberate stress test for the student's categories. State explicitly when none of these strategies is feasible.</p>\n<h3>Annotated investigation notebook</h3>\n<p>Start a new notebook entry titled <em>Probability in pedigrees: prior expectation, actual measurement, alternate mechanism</em>. Record the outcome before labeling it a confirmation or discrepancy.</p>\n<p>For the next pass, consider the topic <strong>sex-linked inheritance</strong>. Review its own mechanistic discussion before assuming a relationship. Ask whether it changes the apparent prediction for <strong>probability in pedigrees</strong>, changes only what is measured, or concerns a different scientific level entirely.</p>\n<h3>A second, more demanding application</h3>\n<p>The memo must discuss <strong>probability in pedigrees</strong> using this design constraint: Draw a three-generation synthetic pedigree with uncertain genotypes, write a likelihood for each inheritance model, and update with a molecular test whose sensitivity and specificity are stated. What would a null result say about assay power?</p>\n<p>The main limitation for this subsection is not decorative fine print: Pedigree symbols do not encode penetrance, adoption, misattributed parentage, mosaicism or phenocopies automatically.</p>\n<h3>Connection to the next course topic</h3>\n<p>A later unit investigates <strong>copy number and dosage</strong>, whose underlying level of analysis should be inspected in that section.</p>\n",
