          "secNumber": "2.5",
          "heading": "Unit overview",
          "content": "A chromosome is a physical carrier of hereditary information, and its different properties\u2014centromere count, DNA mass, homologous sets and sequence content\u2014must not be collapsed into one number. Reproduction, cell division and somatic variation introduce different routes to altered dosage. Cytogenetic descriptions often concern preparations enriched for a particular cell-cycle stage; population statements require considering tissues, selection and mosaicism. Connect each observed rearrangement to the gamete and cellular outcomes it could plausibly generate.",
