          "heading": "Unit overview",
          "content": "Genetic maps describe recombination behavior; physical maps describe DNA coordinates. Neither measurement is a direct substitute for causal gene identification. Linkage requires phase, suitable family or cross data, defined markers and careful treatment of errors. Association across a population introduces a different probability model, influenced by ancestry and demography. This unit uses explicit denominators to prevent percentages of recombinants, centimorgans, LOD evidence and allele associations from being mistakenly interpreted as the same quantity.",
