          "secNumber": "4.5",
          "heading": "Unit overview",
          "content": "Molecular genetics links genotype to function through RNA, proteins and molecular networks. A DNA difference can fail to alter expression, a measured expression difference may not produce a trait, and a phenotype may arise from interaction among several components. The best causal explanations are supported by well-controlled perturbation and rescue rather than annotation alone. Follow genotype verification, product abundance, functional assay and organismal response as distinct measurements with distinct sources of error.",
